§ `Chapters 2 to 8 -- heirs, wardship, marriage and widows`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- the relief an heir pays`

-- gloss (not the text's): "relief" is the sum an heir pays to take up the inheritance.
-- The text says "any of our earls or barons, or others holding of us in chief by military
-- service": whether "in chief by military service" also qualifies earls and barons is
-- fork F2.  The broader reading is taken.
-- src:11 | If any of our earls or barons, or others holding of us in chief by military service shall have died, and at the time of his death his heir shall be of full age and owe “relief,” he shall have his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief, namely
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.1 (src:11)
GIVEN `earl or baron` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holds of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` IF
       `earl or baron`
    OR `holds of the King in chief by military service`

-- src:11 | If any of our earls or barons, or others holding of us in chief by military service shall have died, and at the time of his death his heir shall be of full age and owe “relief,” he shall have his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief, namely
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.1 (src:11)
GIVEN `holder is an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holder held of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holder has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir is of full age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir owes relief` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir has paid the ancient relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` IS
    IF `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` `holder is an earl or a baron` `holder held of the King in chief by military service`
    THEN IF   `holder has died`
          AND `heir is of full age`
          AND `heir owes relief`
         THEN IF `heir has paid the ancient relief`
              THEN Entitled
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because the "if" clause is met here and the case turns on "on payment of the ancient relief", which says what the heir has once he pays and is not a named word (F64c)).
              ELSE `Entitlement not covered`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any of our earls or barons, or others holding of us in chief by military service shall have died, and at the time of his death his heir shall be of full age and owe".
         ELSE `Not entitled`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because the "if" clause names who it speaks of, an earl, a baron or another holder in chief by military service, and the branch is reached by a holder it does not name).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- The sums the text names.  "100s. at most" is a ceiling; the two £100 sums are read as
-- flat sums unless less is owed (fork F2b).
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of an earl, £100 for a whole earl’s barony;
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of a baron, £100 for a whole barony;
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of a knight, 100s. at most for a whole knight’s fee;
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.2-2.4 (src:11)
GIVEN kind IS A HoldingKind
GIVETH A Sterling
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a whole earl's barony` THEN Pounds 100
    WHEN `a whole barony` THEN Pounds 100
    WHEN `a whole knight's fee` THEN Shillings 100

-- src:11 | and whoever owes less let him give less, according to the ancient custom of fiefs.
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.5 (src:11)
GIVEN named IS A NUMBER
      `owed by custom` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the named sum, or less if less is owed` IS
    CONSIDER `owed by custom`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN named
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x LESS THAN named THEN x ELSE named

-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of a knight, 100s. at most for a whole knight’s fee;
-- src:11 | and whoever owes less let him give less, according to the ancient custom of fiefs.
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.4-2.5 (src:11)
GIVEN `owed by custom` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Sterling
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the knight's relief, which is 100s at most` IS
    CONSIDER `owed by custom`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "100s. at most" states a ceiling and no sum when nothing less is owed by custom (F2b).
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (Shillings (IF x LESS THAN 100 THEN x ELSE 100))

-- gloss (not the text's): `owed by custom` is the sum the ancient custom of the fief
-- makes the heir owe when that is less than the sum named; NOTHING when the heir does
-- not owe less.  For a knight's fee the text names only a ceiling, so with nothing owed
-- by custom it states no sum and the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of an earl, £100 for a whole earl’s barony;
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of a baron, £100 for a whole barony;
-- src:11 | the heir or heirs of a knight, 100s. at most for a whole knight’s fee;
-- src:11 | and whoever owes less let him give less, according to the ancient custom of fiefs.
@ref Chapter 2 clause 2.2-2.5 (src:11)
GIVEN kind IS A HoldingKind
      `owed by custom` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Sterling
DECIDE `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a whole earl's barony` THEN JUST (Pounds (`ch 2 -- the named sum, or less if less is owed` 100 `owed by custom`))
    WHEN `a whole barony` THEN JUST (Pounds (`ch 2 -- the named sum, or less if less is owed` 100 `owed by custom`))
    WHEN `a whole knight's fee` THEN `ch 2 -- the knight's relief, which is 100s at most` `owed by custom`

§§ `Chapter 3 -- no relief and no fine for an heir who was in wardship`

-- src:13 | If, however, the heir of any one of the aforesaid has been under age and in wardship, let him have his inheritance without relief and without fine when he comes of age.
@ref Chapter 3 (src:13)
GIVEN `holder is an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holder held of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir was a minor in wardship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir has come of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` IS
    IF `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` `holder is an earl or a baron` `holder held of the King in chief by military service`
    THEN IF `heir was a minor in wardship`
         THEN IF `heir has come of age`
              THEN Barred
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because the "if" clause is met here and the case turns on "when he comes of age", which is not a named word).
              ELSE `Bar not covered`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, however, the heir of any one of the aforesaid has been under age and in wardship".
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because the "if" clause speaks of the heir of "any one of the aforesaid", the holders of chapter 2, and the branch is reached by an heir of a holder it does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- The text says "let him have his inheritance without relief and without fine" and names
-- no one; the holders concerned hold "of us in chief", so the duty is put on the King (fork F3).
-- src:13 | If, however, the heir of any one of the aforesaid has been under age and in wardship, let him have his inheritance without relief and without fine when he comes of age.
@ref Chapter 3 (src:13)
GIVEN `holder is an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holder held of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir was a minor in wardship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heir has come of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 3 -- the heir shall have his inheritance without relief and without fine` IS
    IF `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` `holder is an earl or a baron` `holder held of the King in chief by military service` `heir was a minor in wardship` `heir has come of age` EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         SHANT `demand relief or a fine from an heir who was a minor in wardship`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 3: relief or a fine was demanded of an heir who had been a minor in wardship"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Chapter 4 -- what the guardian may take, and waste`

-- src:15 | The guardian of the land of an heir who is thus under age, shall take from the land of the heir nothing but reasonable produce, reasonable customs, and reasonable services, and that without destruction or waste of men or goods;
@ref Chapter 4 clause 4.1 (src:15)
GIVEN `what is taken is more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the taking is with destruction or waste of men or goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` IS
    IF   `what is taken is more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services`
      OR `the taking is with destruction or waste of men or goods`
    THEN Barred
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing but reasonable produce, reasonable customs, and reasonable services" closes the list, and "that without destruction or waste".
    ELSE `Not barred`

-- src:15 | The guardian of the land of an heir who is thus under age, shall take from the land of the heir nothing but reasonable produce, reasonable customs, and reasonable services, and that without destruction or waste of men or goods;
@ref Chapter 4 clause 4.1 (src:15)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall take from the land nothing but reasonable produce, customs and services` IS
    PARTY `a guardian`
    SHANT `take from the heir's land more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a guardian` BECAUSE "ch 4: the guardian took more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services"

-- src:15 | The guardian of the land of an heir who is thus under age, shall take from the land of the heir nothing but reasonable produce, reasonable customs, and reasonable services, and that without destruction or waste of men or goods;
@ref Chapter 4 clause 4.1 (src:15)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall not make destruction or waste of men or goods` IS
    PARTY `a guardian`
    SHANT `make destruction or waste of the men or goods of the wardship`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a guardian` BECAUSE "ch 4: the guardian made destruction or waste of the men or goods of the wardship"

-- The text does not say who commits or transfers the land (passive); fork F4.
-- src:15 | and if we have committed the wardship of the lands of any such minor to the sheriff, or to any other who is responsible to us for its issues, and he has made destruction or waste of what he holds in wardship, we will take of him amends,
-- src:15 | and the land shall be committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee, who shall be responsible to us for the issues, or to him to whom we shall assign them;
-- src:15 | and if we have given or sold the wardship of any such land to someone and he has therein made destruction or waste, he shall lose that wardship, and it shall be transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief, who shall be responsible to us in like manner as aforesaid.
@ref Chapter 4 clause 4.2-4.4 (src:15)
GIVEN how IS A GuardianKind
GIVETH A WasteConsequence
DECIDE `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` IS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` THEN `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee`
    WHEN `given or sold by the King to someone` THEN `The wardship is lost and transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief`

-- src:15 | and if we have committed the wardship of the lands of any such minor to the sheriff, or to any other who is responsible to us for its issues, and he has made destruction or waste of what he holds in wardship, we will take of him amends,
-- src:15 | and the land shall be committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee, who shall be responsible to us for the issues, or to him to whom we shall assign them;
-- src:15 | and if we have given or sold the wardship of any such land to someone and he has therein made destruction or waste, he shall lose that wardship, and it shall be transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief, who shall be responsible to us in like manner as aforesaid.
@ref Chapter 4 clause 4.2-4.4 (src:15)
GIVEN how IS A GuardianKind
      `the guardian has made destruction or waste` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A WasteConsequence
DECIDE `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` IS
    IF `the guardian has made destruction or waste`
    THEN `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` how
    ELSE `Nothing follows under chapter 4`

§§ `Chapter 5 -- upkeep and restoration of the land`

-- src:17 | The guardian, moreover, so long as he has the wardship of the land, shall keep up the houses, parks, places for live-stock, fishponds, mills, and other things pertaining to the land, out of the issues of the same land;
