    AND `the stocking is as the season of husbandry requires and the issues of the land can reasonably bear`

§§ `Chapter 6 -- the marriage of heirs`

-- The text says "Heirs shall be married" and names no one who marries them (fork F6).
-- gloss (not the text's): "disparagement" is a marriage beneath the heir's rank; whether a
-- marriage is one is a judgment, taken as a plain input.
-- src:19 | Heirs shall be married without disparagement, yet so that before the marriage takes place the nearest in blood to that heir shall have notice.
@ref Chapter 6 (src:19)
GIVEN `the marriage is a disparagement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nearest in blood to the heir has had notice before the marriage takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` IS
    IF   `the marriage is a disparagement`
      OR (NOT `the nearest in blood to the heir has had notice before the marriage takes place`)
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "without disparagement, yet so that ... notice" states what bars a marriage; it does not say that a marriage meeting both is allowed (F64c).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 7 -- the widow's portion, dower and the forty days`

-- The text says the widow "shall ... have" and "shall be assigned" and names no one who
-- must give or assign (fork F7).
-- src:21 | A widow, after the death of her husband, shall forthwith and without difficulty have her marriage portion and inheritance;
@ref Chapter 7 clause 7.1 (src:21)
GIVEN `her husband has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 7 -- the widow may be kept waiting or put to difficulty over her marriage portion and inheritance` IS
    IF `her husband has died`
    THEN Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:21 | nor shall she give anything for her dower, or for her marriage portion, or for the inheritance which her husband and she held on the day of the death of that husband;
@ref Chapter 7 clause 7.2 (src:21)
GIVEN `her husband has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what is asked of her` IS A Demand
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` IS
    IF `her husband has died`
    THEN CONSIDER `what is asked of her`
         -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the cases above and does not close the list with "only".
         WHEN `some other payment` THEN `Bar not covered`
         OTHERWISE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- "forty days": the day of death is day 0 and day 40 is the last day of the forty (fork F7b).
-- src:21 | and she may remain in the house of her husband for forty days after his death,
-- src:21 | within which time her dower shall be assigned to her.
@ref Chapter 7 clause 7.3-7.4 (src:21)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ch 7 -- the number of days the widow may remain in her husband's house, within which her dower is assigned` MEANS 40

-- src:21 | and she may remain in the house of her husband for forty days after his death,
@ref Chapter 7 clause 7.3 (src:21)
GIVEN `days since her husband's death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` IS
    IF   `days since her husband's death` AT LEAST 0
     AND `days since her husband's death` AT MOST `ch 7 -- the number of days the widow may remain in her husband's house, within which her dower is assigned`
    THEN Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "for forty days after his death" gives leave for forty days; the text says nothing about the forty-first day or a day before the death (F7b, F64c).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- src:21 | within which time her dower shall be assigned to her.
@ref Chapter 7 clause 7.4 (src:21)
GIVEN `days since her husband's death when her dower is assigned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 7 -- her dower is assigned within the forty days` IF
        `days since her husband's death when her dower is assigned` AT LEAST 0
    AND `days since her husband's death when her dower is assigned` AT MOST `ch 7 -- the number of days the widow may remain in her husband's house, within which her dower is assigned`

§§ `Chapter 8 -- no widow compelled to marry`

-- The text says "Let no widow be compelled" and names no one who compels (fork F8).
-- src:23 | Let no widow be compelled to marry, so long as she prefers to live without a husband;
-- src:23 | provided always that she gives security not to marry without our consent, if she holds of us, or without the consent of the lord of whom she holds, if she holds of another.
@ref Chapter 8 (src:23)
GIVEN `she is a widow` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she prefers to live without a husband` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she gives security not to marry without the required consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` IS
    IF `she is a widow`
    THEN IF   `she prefers to live without a husband`
          AND `she gives security not to marry without the required consent`
         THEN Barred
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as she prefers to live without a husband" and "provided always that she gives security".
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, so long as, provided because the words qualify what a widow prefers and gives; the branch is reached by a person who is not a widow, whom the sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:23 | provided always that she gives security not to marry without our consent, if she holds of us, or without the consent of the lord of whom she holds, if she holds of another.
@ref Chapter 8 clause 8.2 (src:23)
GIVEN `she holds of the King` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ConsentOf
DECIDE `ch 8 -- the consent her security is against` IS
    IF `she holds of the King`
    THEN `the King's consent`
    ELSE `the consent of the lord of whom she holds`
